{"id":"NCT07225946","title":"A Study of Pasritamig With Docetaxel Versus Docetaxel in Participants With Metastatic Castration-Resistant Prostate Cancer","official":"A Phase 3 Randomized, Open-label Study of Pasritamig (JNJ-78278343), a T-cell-engaging Agent Targeting Human Kallikrein 2, With Docetaxel Versus Docetaxel for Metastatic Castration-resistant Prostate Cancer","summary":"The purpose of this study is to find out whether treatment with pasritamig and docetaxel prolongs radiographic progression free survival (rPFS) (the length of time from start of treatment until disease worsens as determined by scans or death due to any cause) when compared to treatment with docetaxel in participants with metastatic castrate-resistant prostate cancer (mCRPC; a cancer of prostate, a male reproductive gland found below the bladder, that grows despite low levels of male hormones).","conditions":["Prostatic Neoplasms, Castration-Resistant"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Pasritamig"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Docetaxel"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Prednisone/Prednisolone"}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\n\n* Have histologically confirmed adenocarcinoma of the prostate\n* Have disease that is metastatic at the time of screening by computed tomography (CT) or magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) and 99m\\^Tc bone scan as determined by the investigator\n* Participants must receive ongoing androgen deprivation therapy (ADT) with a gonadotropin releasing hormone (GnRH) analog throughout the treatment or have had prior bilateral orchiectomy, and have serum testosterone less than or equal to (\\<=) 50 nanogram per deciliter (ng/dL) (\\<= 1.73 nanomoles per Liter \\[nmol/L\\]) at screening\n* Have progressed by PSA or CT/MRI or 99m\\^Tc bone scan on at least 1 novel androgen receptor pathway inhibition (ARPI) but no more than 2 different ARPI for any stage of disease. Must have discontinued ARPI before randomization into the study\n* Have an eastern cooperative oncology group (ECOG) performance status of 0 to 1\n\nExclusion criteria:\n\n* Known history of either brain or leptomeningeal prostate cancer metastases\n* Participants with known breast cancer gene 1/2 (BRCA 1/2) mutations (germline or somatic) who have not received treatment with a poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase (PARP) inhibitor, unless not available or contraindicated\n* Prior or concurrent second malignancy (other than the disease under study)\n* Received cytotoxic chemotherapy for prostate cancer in any setting\n* Received prior treatment with human kallikrein 2 (KLK-2) directed therapies","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":800,"start":"2025-12-19","pcd":"2027-11-19","upd":"2026-11-03","sponsor":"Janssen Research & Development, LLC","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Study Contact · 844-434-4210 · Participate-In-This-Study1@its.jnj.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Arizona Clinical Trials","city":"Chandler","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85225","s":"R","lat":33.3062,"lon":-111.8413,"c":""},{"f":"Arkansas Urology","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72211","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":""},{"f":"Highlands Oncology Group","city":"Springdale","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72762","s":"R","lat":36.1867,"lon":-94.1288,"c":""},{"f":"MemorialCare Orange Coast Medical Center","city":"Fountain Valley","pr":"California","zip":"92708","s":"R","lat":33.7092,"lon":-117.9537,"c":""},{"f":"University Of California San Diego","city":"La Jolla","pr":"California","zip":"92037","s":"R","lat":32.8473,"lon":-117.2742,"c":""},{"f":"Cancer and Blood Specialty Clinic","city":"Los Alamitos","pr":"California","zip":"90720","s":"R","lat":33.8031,"lon":-118.0726,"c":""},{"f":"USC Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90033","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":""},{"f":"Valkyrie Clinical Trials","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90067","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"